  "response": "**VERDICT: REVISE**\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The carousel implements basic interactive semantics (`<button>`, `aria-label`, `alt`) but fails to meet the WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices Guide Carousel pattern. Core state changes (slide transitions, active indicator) are not communicated to assistive technology, the container lacks required ARIA roles for context, and keyboard navigation is missing. These are design gaps that pass automated linting but break screen reader and keyboard-only user experiences.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**: Before reading code, I predicted: (1) Missing `aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"` and `role=\"group\"` on the container, (2) No `aria-live` region for dynamic slide announcements, (3) Indicator buttons lack programmatic active state (`aria-pressed`/`aria-current`), (4) Missing arrow key/Home/End keyboard navigation per APG. All predictions were confirmed during investigation.\n\n**Critical Findings**: None rated CRITICAL under this component's scope (no complete access loss or data/safety risk). Issues are MAJOR due to significant degradation of AT experience and pattern incompleteness.\n\n**Major Findings** (significantly degrades experience):\n1. **Missing carousel container semantics**\n   - Evidence: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:17` (`<div className=\"carousel\">`) lacks `role=\"group\"` and `aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"`.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users lose context about what the region is and how many slides exist.\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern requires `role=\"group\"` with `aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"` on the container. WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value).\n   - Fix: Add `role=\"group\" aria-roledescription=\"carousel\" aria-label=\"Image carousel\"` to the container `<div>`.\n\n2. **No programmatic announcement of slide changes**\n   - Evidence: No `aria-live` region exists in the component. When `currentIndex` updates, only the DOM image source changes.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users will not know the image changed unless they manually tab through or rely on visual cues.\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern requires an `aria-live=\"polite\"` region to announce slide transitions. WCAG 4.1.3 (Status Messages).\n   - Fix: Add `<div aria-live=\"polite\" className=\"sr-only\">Image {currentIndex + 1} of {images.length}</div>` and update its text content on index change.\n\n3. **Indicator buttons lack active state communication**\n   - Evidence: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:34-40` indicator buttons only toggle a CSS `.active` class. No ARIA attribute reflects the current slide.\n   - User group impacted: Screen reader users hear identical announcements for all indicators; keyboard users relying on AT cannot distinguish the active slide.\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern requires `aria-pressed=\"true\"` (or `aria-current=\"page\"`) on the active indicator. WCAG 4.1.2.\n   - Fix: Add `aria-pressed={idx === currentIndex}` to each indicator button. Update screen reader text or rely on `aria-pressed` state change announcements.\n\n4. **Missing keyboard navigation for carousel controls**\n   - Evidence: Navigation relies solely on click events (`onClick={goToPrevious}`, `onClick={goToNext}`). No keydown handlers for ArrowLeft/ArrowRight, Home, or End.\n   - User group impacted: Keyboard-only users cannot navigate the carousel efficiently; must tab through all buttons sequentially.\n   - WCAG/APG citation: WAI-ARIA APG Carousel Pattern requires arrow keys to move slides, Home/End for first/last slide. WCAG 2.1.1 (Keyboard).\n   - Fix: Add `onKeyDown` handlers to the container or navigation buttons mapping ArrowLeft/Right to prev/next, Home/End to index 0/images.length-1. Ensure focus remains on the trigger button per APG.\n\n**Minor Findings** (friction but workaround exists):\n- **Generic alt text strategy**: `src/components/BuggyCarousel.jsx:21` uses `alt={`Carousel image ${currentIndex + 1}`}`. While functional, it provides no semantic context about the image content. If images have descriptive captions or titles, pass them as props or use `aria-describedby` to link to a caption element. WCAG 1.1.1.\n\n**Enhancements** (best practice not met):\n- Add `aria-label=\"Pause carousel\"` / `aria-label=\"Resume carousel\"` toggle button if auto-play is added later.\n- Ensure focus indicators on buttons meet WCAG 2.4.13 (2px perimeter, 3:1 contrast change).\n- Consider `aria-disabled` on Previous/Next buttons when at first/last slide to prevent redundant navigation.\n\n**What's Missing** (gaps, unhandled edge cases, unstated assumptions):\n- Missing `aria-roledescription=\"carousel\"` and `role=\"group\"` on the container region\n- Missing `aria-live` region for dynamic content announcements\n- Missing `aria-pressed`/`aria-current` on indicator buttons to communicate active state\n- Missing keyboard navigation (arrow keys, Home/End) required by APG Carousel pattern\n- Missing pause/resume control infrastructure (if auto-play is introduced later)\n- No visual focus indicators defined in provided code (assumed CSS-dependent; verify at 3:1 contrast)\n\n**Multi-Perspective Notes**:\n- **Screen reader user**: Hears \"Previous image button\", \"Next image button\", indicator numbers. Carousel context is lost without `role=\"group\"`/`aria-roledescription`. Slide changes are silent unless a live region is added. Active indicator state is invisible to AT.\n- **Keyboard-only user**: Can tab to buttons and click them. No arrow key shortcuts. Focus stays on the clicked button (acceptable but inefficient for complex widgets). Home/End navigation missing.\n- **Low vision user (200% zoom, high contrast)**: Depends on external CSS. Ensure `.active` class has sufficient visual distinction beyond color alone. Verify focus indicators meet 3:1 threshold. Touch targets appear standard but require verification at 44x44px minimum.\n- **Cognitive accessibility**: Labels are clear and consistent. Interaction model is straightforward. Missing active state indication for AT users creates cognitive load for screen reader users trying to track position.\n\n**Verdict Justification**: The component implements ~60% of the WAI-ARIA APG Carousel pattern. Automated checks will likely pass because native `<button>` and `<img>` semantics are present, but assistive technology cannot perceive dynamic state changes or container context. The missing `aria-live` region, active indicator state, carousel role, and keyboard navigation collectively degrade the experience for screen reader and keyboard users. These are design gaps, not visual polish issues. Severity calibrated to MAJOR: realistic worst case is AT users unable to track slide position or navigate efficiently; detection would occur in user testing or bug reports; fix requires adding ARIA attributes and key handlers, not structural overhaul. Upgrades to ACCEPT only after implementing live region, active state, container roles, and keyboard navigation.\n\n**Open Questions (unscored)**:\n- Are the `images` array items expected to have descriptive captions? If so, should they be linked via `aria-describedby` rather than relying solely on `alt`?\n- Is auto-play intended for future implementation? If yes, does it pause on focus/hover and respect `prefers-reduced-motion`?\n- What is the external CSS for `.active`? Does it rely solely on color change, or does it include shape/position/text changes to satisfy WCAG 1.4.1 (non-color indicator)?",
